d lane won't have those tools. Copying the file would give the agent's shell a readable copy of the home config, so I left it out. If the comparison needs those tools, that's a decision for you.\n\n## Colleague's note: what applied\n\n- **Applied:** the sandbox denies reads and writes under the real home, so the Codex output file goes to a scratch folder in `/tmp`, and the lane copies it into the run folder afterwards. stdout and stderr still go straight into the run folder. Don't trust exit 0: the lane now logs a missing last-message file to `agent.err`.\n- **Did not apply (not in this repo):** Mistral Vibe and its `--output-dir` flag. This harness has no Vibe lane.\n- **Applied as a precaution, not as a fix here:** this repo lives at `/private/tmp/h-A7v2QM`, outside the real home, so the `-o` denial the colleague hit wouldn't happen in this layout. I used the scratch folder anyway, so the lane still works if the run folder ever moves under the home folder.\n- **Did not apply:** the colleague's specific failure was a run folder under the home folder, which isn't this setup. I didn't change the profile or the `kimi` lane.\n\nNothing was committed, deployed, published, or sent to any external service.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":7,"newStart":24,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## What differs from the `codex` lane"," ","-- `~/.codex/config.toml` is not copied into the scratch `CODEX_HOME`, so this lane runs with Codex defaults plus the env key. The real config has no model setting but does enable the github and posthog plugins and an MCP server under the home folder. The sandboxed lane won't have those tools. Copying the file would give the agent's shell a readable copy of the home config, so I left it out. If the comparison needs those tools, that's a decision for you.","+- `~/.codex/config.toml` is not copied into the scratch `CODEX_HOME`, so this lane runs with Codex defaults plus the env key. The real config sets no model or provider (I checked), but it enables the github and posthog plugins and defines two MCP servers, `pencil` (under the home folder) and `posthog`. The sandboxed lane won't have those tools. Copying the file would give the agent's shell a readable copy of the home config, so I left it out. If the comparison needs those tools, that's a decision for you."," "," ## Colleague's note: what applied"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M96RCnvx6etJhzXLc5v6qN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtSFrEWqW3vNrQJz6caD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same Codex command as the `codex` lane inside `sandbox/agent.sb`, the way `kimi` does. I tested it with a stub `codex`; I did not run a live Codex job, since that would send the task to OpenAI and you hadn't asked for that.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`run.sh`**: the new lane gives Codex an empty scratch `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME`, so it can't see `~/.codex`. `-o` writes to a scratch folder in `/tmp`, and the lane copies `final.txt` into the run folder after the sandbox exits. If Codex exits 0 without writing that file, the lane logs it to `agent.err`.\n- **`README.md`**: one bullet for the new lane.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`** and the existing `codex` and `kimi` lanes are unchanged.\n- **`ANSWER.md`**: written up, including which parts of the colleague's note applied.\n\n**Verification**\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n- The sandbox denies reads of `~/.codex/config.toml` and writes to the real home. Writes to scratch paths succeed, and the sandboxed `codex --version` runs.\n- A stub-`codex` run of `fizz` produced `final.txt`, `answer.json`, and `exit_code: 0`. I deleted that test folder afterwards.\n\n**Not verified**\n- **Authentication.** The README says Codex logs in with `CODEX_API_KEY`. That variable isn't set in my shell, so I couldn't confirm it. `~/.codex/auth.json` exists. If the login depends on that file, the sandboxed lane will fail to authenticate. I didn't open `auth.json` to the sandbox, because the agent's shell could then read the credential.\n- **Config differences.** I didn't copy `config.toml`, so this lane lacks the github and posthog plugins and the `pencil` and `posthog` MCP servers that the `codex` lane loads. If the comparison needs them, that's your call.\n\n**Colleague's note**\n- **Applied:** the scratch-folder pattern for the `-o` output, and the rule that exit 0 doesn't prove the output was written.\n- **Not applicable:** Mistral Vibe isn't in this harness. This repo also sits outside the real home, so the `-o` denial they hit wouldn't occur here. I used the scratch folder anyway, as a precaution.\n\nNothing was committed or sent anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":45361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":459},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"010ecbb7-a11c-48d4-8b56-60f51d795b89","uuid":"a0cd97fc-d5e4-438e-b2fa-64f8b019f845","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:11:27.669Z","request_id":"req_011CgtSFr5r8HEUSzq7g41Ln"}
